00:21:39.500 --> 00:21:40.680
Yeah.
What about linear combinations?

00:21:40.960 --> 00:21:44.720
Yeah, I should always think of
this as a linear combination of

00:21:44.720 --> 00:21:46.860
the matrix's columns.

00:21:46.860 --> 00:21:49.180
So even knowing nothing about
the matrix,

00:21:49.180 --> 00:21:51.900
if you see A times 3, 2,

00:21:51.900 --> 00:21:52.980
what you should think of is,

00:21:52.980 --> 00:21:53.400
OK,

00:21:53.400 --> 00:21:56.640
all I'm asking for here is 3
times A's first column plus 2

00:21:56.640 --> 00:21:58.300
times its second column.

00:21:58.300 --> 00:22:00.420
But what do you notice here?

00:22:00.420 --> 00:22:03.760
3 times A's first column is 12,
negative 6.

00:22:03.760 --> 00:22:09.010
And 2 times its second column is
